&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Overview&#8232;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
IN-PERSON &amp;amp; VIRTUAL CONFERENCE&lt;br /&gt;
Columbia University Medical Center invites you to join the leading clinician-educators from Columbia University, addressing current and future breakthroughs in Lupus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;In-person registration includes light breakfast and lunch&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Objectives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand Current Guidelines and Advances in Lupus Nephritis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Explore the latest guidelines for diagnosing and managing lupus nephritis, along with insights into emerging research and therapeutic approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assess the Role of CAR T Cell Therapy in Autoimmune Diseases&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Analyze the mechanisms, applications, and evolving landscape of CAR T cell therapy, particularly in autoimmune diseases like lupus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate Artificial Intelligence and Novel Technologies in Lupus Care&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Examine the potential of AI, virtual reality, and advanced imaging technologies to transform lupus diagnosis, monitoring, and treatment strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify Genetic and Immunophenotypic Predictors of Lupus Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Evaluate the impact of genetic and immunophenotypic markers on predicting renal disease and guiding personalized treatment approaches in lupus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore Innovations and Challenges in Lupus Clinical Trials&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Review cutting-edge therapies and strategies in lupus clinical trials, focusing on cardiovascular disease, immunophenotyping, and novel treatment targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video Access&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Following the program, all registrants will have access to lecture video recordings for ONE month.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Svetla Marinova &amp;rsquo;11GSAS, Strategic Partnerships Specialist at Microsoft, kicks off Season Three of&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;She Opened the Door: Ask the Expert&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;with a candid conversation on navigating a career in big tech. Svetla&amp;rsquo;s journey has spanned capital markets, cloud innovation, and fintech&amp;mdash;building a dynamic, purpose-driven career that didn&amp;rsquo;t always follow a straight line. From arriving in the U.S. as an international student, to breaking into competitive industries, to learning how to trust her intuition in high-stakes environments, Svetla offers real insight into the evolving realities of work and leadership today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us for a conversation about finding your place in uncertain times, cultivating long-term relationships, and opening doors for yourself&amp;mdash;and others&amp;mdash;along the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

